{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_all_of_all_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_all_of_all_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyReduction.lean#L103-L113","doc":"**The reduction, stated as one hypothesis.**  If every adjacent pair commutes, the whole JM\nfamily is commutative.\n\nWhen this was written the hypothesis was the open residue for `i ≥ 2`.  It is **no longer open**:\n[`HeckeTranspositionExpansion.jmRaw_comm_adjacent`](HeckeTranspositionExpansion.lean) discharges it\noutright, via the additive family and Jucys's telescoping, so `jmRaw_comm_all` in that file is this\nconclusion with no hypothesis at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_one_comm_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_one_comm_all","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyReduction.lean#L95-L101","doc":"**The `i = 1` row is complete**: `L₂` commutes with every `Lⱼ`.\n\n`jmRaw_comm_adjacent_one` supplies the adjacent case at `i = 1`; the reduction propagates it to all\n`j`.  This upgrades what was a single instance into a full row of the commutativity matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_of_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_of_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyReduction.lean#L66-L93","doc":"**Adjacent commutativity implies all of it.**  If `Lᵢ` commutes with `L_{i+1}`, it commutes with\nevery `Lⱼ` for `j ≥ i`.  Induction on `j`, each step conjugating by `σⱼ` via\n`jmRaw_commutator_step`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_commutator_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_commutator_step","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyReduction.lean#L49-L64","doc":"**The commutator reduction.**  For `j > i`, `[Lᵢ, L_{j+1}] = σⱼ [Lᵢ, Lⱼ] σⱼ`.\n\n`L_{j+1} = σⱼLⱼσⱼ`, and `j > i` lets `Lᵢ` slide past both copies of `σⱼ` by far-commutation.  So a\nfar commutator is a conjugate of the one a step closer — no cancellation, no Hecke relation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}